WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.502
-Hello, everyone,
and welcome to another

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:05.405
special social distancing
episode of "Late Night."

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:08.975
As you can see
from the backdrop behind me,

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:11.911
I have moved from my hallway
to my private study

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:14.146
where I sit at night
in a smoking jacket

00:00:14.146 --> 00:00:16.950
with a glass of brandy pondering
life's great mysteries.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:21.087
It looks kind of like this.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:23.656
Eureka.
And as you can also see,

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:27.259
I own my very own
"back in my day" sweater

00:00:27.259 --> 00:00:31.831
that I wear unironically,
so ya burnt! me.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:34.667
And to be clear, this is
definitely my private study

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:37.603
and not a garage I've been
relegated to

00:00:37.603 --> 00:00:39.739
because my family has told me
on no uncertain terms

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:42.975
I'm not allowed to do
my little political rants

00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:44.110
at the dinner table.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.678
Now, I hope you're
all staying at home

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:48.414
self-distancing and doing
your part to slow the spread,

00:00:48.414 --> 00:00:50.316
despite the fact that
our unhinged president

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:51.684
would like to ignore the crisis

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.519
and return to normal
as soon as possible.

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:56.689
For more on this.
It's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:56.689 --> 00:01:00.426 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:02.495
Donald Trump sees everything
as a transaction.

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:05.698
His first question is always,
"What do I get out of this?"

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.934
It's what he asked
when he was building casinos.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:10.637
It's what he asked when they
offered him "The Apprentice,"

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:13.272
and it's what he asked
when Eric was born.

00:01:13.272 --> 00:01:14.607
[ As Trump ] Great.
What's in it for me?

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:15.742
[ Normal voice ] And even
the doctor was like,

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:17.577
"Oh, literally nothing.

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:19.945
Nothing. This is a straight-up
loss for you."

00:01:19.945 --> 00:01:22.015
That's what happened when
he got impeached, remember?

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:22.916
You remember that?

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:25.217
That huge world historical event

00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:30.089
that happened approximately, I
don't know, like 307 years ago.

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:32.425
Talking about the impeachment of
Donald Trump feels like talking

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:35.728
about going to RadioShack
to pick up a Walkman,

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:39.198
to listen to the new
Tears for Fears album.

00:01:39.198 --> 00:01:41.067
"Back in my day."

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:42.201
It was less
than four months ago,

00:01:42.201 --> 00:01:43.102
but it feels like it happened

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:44.770
right around the same time

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:46.739
Trump popped up
in "Home Alone 2."

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:48.207
[ As Trump ] Yeah, I hope
you find your parents, kid,

00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:52.111
but first, you know where I can
get some dirt on Joe Biden?

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:53.613
[ Normal voice ] It feels
impossible to remember this now,

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:57.383
but the federal response to
a deadly and highly infectious

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:59.452
global pandemic is being
overseen by a president

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:01.487
who was impeached less than
four months ago

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:04.990
for trying to use foreign aid
to a war-torn country

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:06.692
to benefit himself politically.

00:02:06.692 --> 00:02:09.394
As you may recall,
immediately after the aid

00:02:09.394 --> 00:02:10.930
came up on his phone call

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:13.465
with the newly elected president
of Ukraine,

00:02:13.465 --> 00:02:15.901
Trump literally said the words,

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:18.971
"I would like you
to do us a favor, though."

00:02:18.971 --> 00:02:20.506
And of course,
Trump is the kind of guy

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:23.742
who asks you for a favor
before he's even met you.

00:02:23.742 --> 00:02:26.512
He's like a guy messaging
a girl he just met on Tinder.

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:27.613
"Would love to meet you.

00:02:27.613 --> 00:02:29.215
Can I crash at your place
for a few days?

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:30.650
I have a fever and a cough.

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:33.052
And my roommate kicked me out
for using their toothbrush.

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:35.922
Also, my roommate is my wife
and I have five kids."

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:38.257
So everything with Trump
is a transaction

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:40.493
in which he seeks
to personally benefit himself,

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:43.128
whether it's foreign aid
to a war-torn country

00:02:43.128 --> 00:02:44.497
or a global pandemic.

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:46.366
For example,
after he was criticized

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:48.767
by New York Governor
Andrew Cuomo for not sending

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:52.104
the state enough ventilators
from the federal stockpile,

00:02:52.104 --> 00:02:55.408
Trump lashed out by claiming it
was a two-way street

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:58.043
and that governors had to earn
help from the federal government

00:02:58.043 --> 00:02:59.278
by being nice to him.

00:02:59.278 --> 00:03:00.480
-We're building them hospitals.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.915
We're building
a medical centers.

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:03.649
And he was complaining
about we're doing

00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:06.919
probably more definitely
more than anybody else.

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:08.387
But he shouldn't
be talking about us.

00:03:08.387 --> 00:03:10.389
He's supposed to be buying
his own ventilators.

00:03:10.389 --> 00:03:13.526
We're going to help.
We're working very, very hard

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:15.961
for the people of New York.
We're working along with him.

00:03:15.961 --> 00:03:18.364
And then I watch him on the show
complaining.

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:20.499
We are doing very well with,
I think,

00:03:20.499 --> 00:03:22.368
almost all of the governors
for the most part.

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:23.636
I think we're doing very well.

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:25.204
But, you know,
it's a two-way street.

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:26.805
They have to treat us well,
also.

00:03:26.805 --> 00:03:28.841
-No, they don't. It's your job.

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:30.843
They don't owe you anything
for doing your job.

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:33.446
States don't pay tribute
to the president.

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.415
[ As Trump ] What gifts have
arrived for me today?

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:37.016
[ Normal voice ] Well,
Mr. President,

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.751
Alaska sent timber.
Maryland sent crabs.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.252
[ As Trump ]
And what of New York?

00:03:40.252 --> 00:03:41.887
[ Normal voice ] They set the
most magnificent creature, sir.

00:03:41.887 --> 00:03:44.156
He is half-man, half-baseball.

00:03:44.156 --> 00:03:47.126
[ As Trump ]
How amusing. Yes. Yes.

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:50.296
Send them two ventilators
in return.

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:51.931
[ Normal voice ]
What makes you like this?

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:53.866
This guy is so insecure
and self-obsessed,

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:55.768
he demands constant praise
and validation

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:57.269
simply for doing
the bare minimum.

00:03:57.269 --> 00:04:00.740
And if he doesn't get it, he'll
just thank himself in a tweet.

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:02.474
Imagine being America's
dumbest person

00:04:02.474 --> 00:04:04.843
somehow getting
the highest office in the land

00:04:04.843 --> 00:04:07.347
and still thinking
you're owed something.

00:04:07.347 --> 00:04:09.381
He's like a dog
who expects a treat

00:04:09.381 --> 00:04:10.650
every time you [bleep]
in the yard.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:11.851
When you let him back
in the house,

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:13.285
he goes straight to the closet
and sits there

00:04:13.285 --> 00:04:15.388
until you toss him a McNugget.

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:17.289
In fact, The Daily Beast
reported this week

00:04:17.289 --> 00:04:20.192
that Trump views his response
to the pandemic

00:04:20.192 --> 00:04:22.695
purely through the lens
of who's being nice to him.

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:24.130
And as a result of that,

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:26.298
he's been swinging wildly
back and forth,

00:04:26.298 --> 00:04:29.135
depending on what Cuomo says
about him on any given day.

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:31.604
A person who spoken to the
president earlier this month

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:33.939
recounted that one day, Trump
had mentioned in a meeting

00:04:33.939 --> 00:04:36.675
how well Cuomo was behaving
in handling the crisis,

00:04:36.675 --> 00:04:39.145
Only to two days later,
start bashing the governor

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:41.847
in a different private
conversation as "nasty."

00:04:41.847 --> 00:04:43.148
There's no telling which Trump

00:04:43.148 --> 00:04:45.084
you're going to get
on any given day.

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:46.385
One day, he'll be
your best friend.

00:04:46.385 --> 00:04:47.686
The next day, he'll hate you.

00:04:47.686 --> 00:04:49.788
It's like we're trapped
in the movie "Fight Club."

00:04:49.788 --> 00:04:51.257
One day,
we're going to see Trump

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:53.392
kicking the crap out himself
in the White House parking lot.

00:04:53.392 --> 00:04:55.628
[ As Trump ]
The first rule of fight club --

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:57.863
I get 20 percent of all bets.

00:04:57.863 --> 00:05:00.065
[ Normal voice ] Also, I really,
truly hate that Trump

00:05:00.065 --> 00:05:02.802
uses the word "nasty" as an
insult because it ruins

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:04.603
what could otherwise be
a fun word.

00:05:04.603 --> 00:05:06.806
Just once, I'd like to see him
get up at the podium

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:08.974
and use it the way
Raven-Symoné would use it.

00:05:08.974 --> 00:05:12.278
[ As Trump ] Everyone remember,
don't cough into your hands

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:13.746
'cause that's nasty!

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:15.013
[ Normal voice ] The president

00:05:15.013 --> 00:05:16.482
is supposed to be
a public trust.

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:18.618
You're supposed to be able
to distinguish between

00:05:18.618 --> 00:05:20.987
your own personal interests
and the duties of the office.

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:23.823
Now, sure, every president
gets something out of it.

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:27.593
Maybe they use it to meet girls
or they get a nice Netflix deal.

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:30.796
They might even use it to score
a sweet job in real estate.

00:05:30.796 --> 00:05:34.434
95 years old
and still building houses.

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:38.203
Jimmy Carter is the yin
to Trump's yang.

00:05:38.203 --> 00:05:39.338
It's like he has to do
a good thing

00:05:39.338 --> 00:05:41.373
for every bad thing Trump does.

00:05:41.373 --> 00:05:42.808
One house at a time.

00:05:42.808 --> 00:05:44.376
Every time Trump tweets,
Jimmy says,

00:05:44.376 --> 00:05:46.679
[ As Carter ]
Better get my tool belt.

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:49.182
[ Normal voice ] So, yes, there
are benefits to being president,

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:50.716
but Trump is taking it
to an insane level.

00:05:50.716 --> 00:05:54.787
He pathologically is incapable
of grasping anything

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:57.223
other than his own survival.
In fact, CNN reported this week

00:05:57.223 --> 00:05:59.992
that Trump is considering
reopening the country

00:05:59.992 --> 00:06:01.994
prematurely in the middle
of a deadly pandemic,

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:06.298
partially because he personally
is bored inside the White House.

00:06:06.298 --> 00:06:08.100
-I want to bring in CNN's
Caitlin Collins

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.301
live for us
from the White House.

00:06:09.301 --> 00:06:11.336
Caitlin, sources tell you
that the president

00:06:11.336 --> 00:06:13.639
is feeling increasingly isolated
at the White House

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:16.408
and questioning, eager
to have life returned to normal.

00:06:16.408 --> 00:06:18.610
-Yeah, he feels like he's been
cut off from the outside world,

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:21.847
much like the rest of the nation
and other parts of the world

00:06:21.847 --> 00:06:23.882
feel as they are responding
to this staying home.

00:06:23.882 --> 00:06:27.687
-Hey, man, welcome to the club.
We're all stuck inside.

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:29.122
Why don't you just
do what we're all doing

00:06:29.122 --> 00:06:30.222
and put on your sweatpants,

00:06:30.222 --> 00:06:31.857
watch four episodes
of "Tiger King,"

00:06:31.857 --> 00:06:33.592
try to do an online workout,
give up,

00:06:33.592 --> 00:06:36.261
and just drink wine out of a
cereal bowl until you pass out.

00:06:36.261 --> 00:06:38.664
You're not the only one
being inconvenienced.

00:06:38.664 --> 00:06:41.033
Normally, I'd be doing my show
from a well-lit studio

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:42.735
in midtown Manhattan
for 200 people,

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:44.170
but instead,
I'm here in my house

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:45.704
trying to get my dog
to laugh at my jokes.

00:06:45.704 --> 00:06:48.641
I got people on Twitter telling
me I'm worse at YouTube videos

00:06:48.641 --> 00:06:51.009
than their teenage daughters.
Well, no [bleep]

00:06:51.009 --> 00:06:53.478
I'm 46, which probably
won't surprise you

00:06:53.478 --> 00:06:54.613
now that you see
what I look like

00:06:54.613 --> 00:06:55.747
when I'm doing my own makeup.

00:06:55.747 --> 00:06:57.817
Also, teenage girls
are great at YouTube

00:06:57.817 --> 00:06:59.618
and I know because I spent
half the day

00:06:59.618 --> 00:07:00.886
watching makeup tutorials

00:07:00.886 --> 00:07:03.589
on how not to look
like a ghost in a bookstore.

00:07:03.589 --> 00:07:06.626
And do you know how hard it is
to tell a 4-year-old

00:07:06.626 --> 00:07:08.360
"Daddy has to go make
one of his videos."

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.496
I mean, it's true,
but it sounds like a lie.

00:07:10.496 --> 00:07:11.664
It sounds like what you'd say

00:07:11.664 --> 00:07:13.566
before going to the garage
to drink alone.

00:07:13.566 --> 00:07:15.501
[ Slurring ]
I gave 'em hell today, buddy.

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:18.037
I gave 'em hell in my video.

00:07:18.037 --> 00:07:19.272
[ Normal voice ] Yesterday,
I had a take ruined

00:07:19.272 --> 00:07:20.839
because a bird wouldn't shut up.

00:07:20.839 --> 00:07:23.042
You know how bad things are when
you're having bird troubles?

00:07:23.042 --> 00:07:25.578
They're bad.
So I'm sorry you're bored,

00:07:25.578 --> 00:07:27.413
stuck in America's
most famous house

00:07:27.413 --> 00:07:29.715
that has its own personal chef
in a bowling alley.

00:07:29.715 --> 00:07:30.849
Boo-hoo.

00:07:30.849 --> 00:07:32.084
In fact, CNN also reported

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:33.853
that Trump is so bored
in the White House

00:07:33.853 --> 00:07:36.522
he's actually been
going to meetings

00:07:36.522 --> 00:07:38.191
like everyone working from home.

00:07:38.191 --> 00:07:39.959
Trump has shown evidence
of cabin fever,

00:07:39.959 --> 00:07:42.194
crashing meetings of
his coronavirus task force,

00:07:42.194 --> 00:07:44.063
inserting himself
in planned press conferences

00:07:44.063 --> 00:07:45.864
during daily policy sessions.

00:07:45.864 --> 00:07:48.034
Aides say they sometimes
don't know whether Trump

00:07:48.034 --> 00:07:49.401
will walk through the door,

00:07:49.401 --> 00:07:51.370
leading to a general level
of uncertainty

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:53.339
on what to place on the agenda.

00:07:53.339 --> 00:07:54.640
So the answer to the riddle,

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:57.042
"How do you get the president
to go to a meeting?"

00:07:57.042 --> 00:07:59.478
is a [bleep] pandemic.

00:07:59.478 --> 00:08:01.313
But of course,
he makes meetings worse.

00:08:01.313 --> 00:08:03.115
It's amazing to think that
if you want to do

00:08:03.115 --> 00:08:05.317
the actual work of government
in the Trump era,

00:08:05.317 --> 00:08:07.686
you have to hide like a teenage
boy with a copy of "Maxim."

00:08:07.686 --> 00:08:09.322
[ Whispering ]
So as you can see here,

00:08:09.322 --> 00:08:10.756
maximizing testing capacity

00:08:10.756 --> 00:08:12.924
is the most efficient way
to flatten the curve --

00:08:12.924 --> 00:08:16.595
Oh, crap! Someone's in here!
Someone's in here!

00:08:16.595 --> 00:08:17.996
[ Normal voice ] And there
must be a huge difference

00:08:17.996 --> 00:08:19.264
between having Trump
in the meeting

00:08:19.264 --> 00:08:20.666
and not having him
in the meeting.

00:08:20.666 --> 00:08:23.502
If he's not there, you can
dive deep into the weeds

00:08:23.502 --> 00:08:25.704
of public health
and epidemiology.

00:08:25.704 --> 00:08:28.307
If he's there, you have to
rewrite the agenda

00:08:28.307 --> 00:08:29.808
so the first item is --

00:08:29.808 --> 00:08:33.512
"Coronavirus. Did Obama start it
alone or did Hillary help?"

00:08:33.512 --> 00:08:35.948
[ As Trump ] My personal take
is it looks like a two-man job.

00:08:35.948 --> 00:08:38.283
But you guys are the scientists.
Okay.

00:08:38.283 --> 00:08:40.152
I'm going to go give
the Lincoln portrait

00:08:40.152 --> 00:08:41.887
another shaving cream beard.

00:08:41.887 --> 00:08:43.622
I'm gonna groom you, Lincoln!

00:08:43.622 --> 00:08:45.524
[ Normal voice ] Also,
it's really gotta suck

00:08:45.524 --> 00:08:46.925
for everyone else
in the White House

00:08:46.925 --> 00:08:48.961
now that Trump is trapped inside
and showing up to meetings.

00:08:48.961 --> 00:08:50.596
it's like trying to
work from home

00:08:50.596 --> 00:08:51.797
while babysitting your kids.

00:08:51.797 --> 00:08:53.599
Next time Mike Pence
Skypes into a meeting,

00:08:53.599 --> 00:08:55.834
Trump's gonna wander
into the room behind him

00:08:55.834 --> 00:08:57.236
in a baby walker.

00:08:57.236 --> 00:09:00.272
Well, Trump apparently
resented the implication

00:09:00.272 --> 00:09:01.707
that he was bored while holed up
in the White House

00:09:01.707 --> 00:09:04.343
because yesterday he lashed out
on Twitter,

00:09:04.343 --> 00:09:07.580
writing "I hear that fake news
CNN just reported

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:09.448
that I am isolated
in the White House,

00:09:09.448 --> 00:09:12.951
wondering out loud when life
will return to normal.

00:09:12.951 --> 00:09:14.419
Does anybody really believe
that?

00:09:14.419 --> 00:09:16.788
There was no leak.
They made it up.

00:09:16.788 --> 00:09:18.624
They are corrupt and fake news.

00:09:18.624 --> 00:09:20.526
I've been packed all day
with meetings.

00:09:20.526 --> 00:09:22.294
I have no time for stupidity."

00:09:22.294 --> 00:09:23.662
This is the age of coronavirus.

00:09:23.662 --> 00:09:25.765
Being packed in meetings
is stupidity.

00:09:25.765 --> 00:09:26.932
[ As Trump ]
So many meetings today.

00:09:26.932 --> 00:09:28.066
Each one with more people.

00:09:28.066 --> 00:09:31.103
Each one in a smaller room,
sharing one pen.

00:09:31.103 --> 00:09:33.205
[ Normal voice ] Stupidity
is all you have time for.

00:09:33.205 --> 00:09:34.639
You spend so much time
on stupidity,

00:09:34.639 --> 00:09:35.874
you literally got the country's

